 // the bit later would leave the actor cached in the old node.
+// [Dauntless Reforged Revival] A dormant weapon must not be filed as a static actor.
+//
+// Every hunt with a hammer (WP_IH_BEGINNER on a new account, WP_IH_ROCK on the old one) times out
+// loading. The server-side [ServerWeaponGap] log (17 Oct, 03:05) shows the hammer equipped and attached
+// to the pawn 150 units away, yet the player's connection has no actor channel for it and has never
+// replicated it (channel=null lastRepFrame=0 for 30 s), while the armour and the lantern, with the same
+// cull distance, replicate every frame. The client therefore never gets a CurrentWeapon.
+//
+// UReplicationGraph::AddNetworkActor (RVA 0xF12D40) sets FGlobalActorReplicationInfo+0x14
+// (bWantsToBeDormant) to NetDormancy (+0xF1) > DORM_Awake and then calls this route function. For an actor
+// with neither bAlwaysRelevant nor bOnlyRelevantToOwner, the route (RVA 0x1BFE430) hands it to the spatial
+// grid's AddActor_Dormancy (RVA 0xF12820), which files a dormant actor with AddActorInternal_Static: the
+// grid cells are picked once, from where the actor is at that moment, and are never updated when it moves.
+// A weapon is spawned before it is attached to its pawn, so a dormant weapon stays filed at its spawn
+// point; a connection only gathers it when its viewer is within the cull distance of that point. In the
+// city that happens to be close enough; on a hunt map the player starts far from it and the weapon is
+// never sent. An awake weapon is filed as a dynamic actor, whose cell follows it every frame, which is
+// what the armour and lantern already are.
+//
+// So a weapon on the spatial route is filed awake: NetDormancy DORM_Awake and bWantsToBeDormant 0, the
+// same state AddNetworkActor writes for an actor that was awake from the start. The weapon then keeps its
+// actor channel instead of going dormant, which costs a little bandwidth for at most one weapon per
+// player. DISABLE_WEAPON_DORMANCY_FIX.flag turns this off (and the tick-time wake in
+// MpWakeUnsentPawnWeapons); the route line is logged either way.
+static bool GetActorWorldLocation(void* Actor, float& X, float& Y, float& Z);
+static bool SafeWriteByte(uintptr_t base, uintptr_t offset, uint8_t value);
+
+static bool MpWeaponDormancyFixEnabled() {
+    static int s_enabled = -1;
+    if (s_enabled < 0) s_enabled = MpExeRelativeFlagPresent(L"DISABLE_WEAPON_DORMANCY_FIX.flag") ? 0 : 1;
+    return s_enabled == 1;
+}
